+### [Sparse Voxel Octree Leaf Population](18654-sparse-voxel-octree-leaf-population.md)
+This method populates the leaf nodes of a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) with voxel color, normal, and irradiance data derived from a flat list of voxel fragments. It serves as the final stage of the SVO construction pipeline, translating raw voxelized geometry into the hierarchical brick structure required for ray-marching or cone-tracing rendering. Unlike sibling methods that focus on octree topology generation or mipmap creation, this step is strictly concerned with data transfer and packing into the leaf-level texture buffers.
+
+### [Sparse Voxel Octree Construction via GPU Coarse-to-Fine Voxelization](21316-sparse-voxel-octree-construction-via-gpu-coarse-to-fine-voxe.md)
+An algorithm to construct a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) from a mesh by iteratively voxelizing the scene at increasing resolutions (coarse nodes), compacting occupied nodes, and building the octree hierarchy level by level on the GPU using thrust scans and custom CUDA kernels. It differs from standard SVO builders by starting with a coarse voxelization of the entire bounding box and refining only occupied regions, reducing memory overhead for sparse scenes compared to dense voxelization approaches.
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear in the number of input voxels for collection and leaf grouping. Iterative layer construction scales with tree depth ($\log_2(\text{size})$). Parent/neighbor filling scales linearly with total node count [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** The flat array `_tree` stores one `uint32_t` per node. The number of nodes depends on the sparsity of the input and the `maxDepth` [S3, unofficial].
